<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Puerta del Conde</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Puerta del Conde is a fortified gate in the colonial walls of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santo-domingo">Santo Domingo</a>, named after the Count of Peñalva, who defended the city against an English attack in 1655. On the night of 27 February 1844 Dominican patriots gathered there to proclaim independence from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haiti">Haiti</a> and raised the first Dominican flag. The adjoining Altar de la Patria holds the remains of the founders Duarte, Sánchez and Mella.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/puerta-del-conde.jpg" alt="Puerta del Conde" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mariordo (Mario Roberto Durán Ortiz) · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Puerta_del_Conde_CCSD_09_2018_1631.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
